1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:11,222
After the burning of the lac house, the five Pāṇḍava brothers lived hidden in the town of Ekacakrā, disguised as brahmins, begging their bread.

2
00:00:11,222 --> 00:00:13,350
But over that town hung a shadow.

3
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:18,834
In the wood lived Bakāsura, a rākṣasa who devoured men.

4
00:00:18,834 --> 00:00:23,611
Each week the town sent him a cartload of food — and the one who drove the cart.

5
00:00:23,611 --> 00:00:28,985
Now the lot fell on the very house that had sheltered them; and the brahmin's family wept.

6
00:00:31,185 --> 00:00:34,110
Then Kuntī said quietly: "Do not grieve.

7
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:39,813
You gave my sons shelter; my son shall take your place." And she chose Bhīma —

8
00:00:39,813 --> 00:00:41,714
the strongest of the five.

9
00:00:44,114 --> 00:00:47,709
At dawn Bhīma drove the loaded cart toward the forest —

10
00:00:47,709 --> 00:00:53,134
and being Bhīma, and being hungry, he ate the demon's dinner himself along the way.

11
00:00:55,933 --> 00:01:01,552
The rākṣasa came roaring from the trees — huge as a hill, furious at the empty cart.

12
00:01:01,552 --> 00:01:07,573
They fought, tree against fist, until Bhīma seized him and broke his back across his knee.

13
00:01:11,573 --> 00:01:18,422
In the morning the people of Ekacakrā found the demon dead at their gates, and wondered who had saved them.

14
00:01:18,422 --> 00:01:20,471
The brahmins kept their secret —

15
00:01:20,471 --> 00:01:25,656
and walked on quietly, toward Pāñcāla, and a destiny that would change the world.
